## 4. Domain Operational Artifacts

### 4.1 Model Cards
Based on customer requirements (CVS, Tesco, Wells Fargo, Microsoft) and internal governance, Model Cards at Atlassian must document:
- **Model details**: Family, developer, version, architecture
- **Intended use**: In-scope/out-of-scope use cases, intended users, deployment regions
- **Training data**: Sources, recency, known gaps, PII handling
- **Factors**: Demographic, environmental, and instrumentation factors affecting results
- **Metrics**: Performance metrics chosen and rationale
- **Evaluation data**: Datasets, representativeness, challenging cases
- **Quantitative analyses**: Performance breakdowns by important factors
- **Ethical considerations**: Sensitive data, implications for safety, bias mitigation
- **Responsible AI alignment**: Fairness, explainability, safety, transparency, sustainability
- **Known limitations and caveats**

### 4.2 Evaluation Reports & Frameworks
- **Offline evaluation suites**: SxS eval on holdout sets with MRR/NDCG/precision@k
- **Win/loss analysis**: Top query examples extracted and sliced by connector type, region
- **Regression gates**: Automated checks before flight promotion
- **LLM judge evaluations**: Custom judges for validating output quality (DeepEval, AIX frameworks)
- **Golden datasets**: Test cases with ground truth for controlled evaluation
- **Production evaluation pipelines**: Continuous monitoring of real-world performance
- **Statistical significance assessments**: p-value reporting for metric movements

### 4.3 Experiment Tracking Artifacts
- **MLflow experiment runs**: Hyperparameters, metrics, model artifacts tracked automatically
- **Training configuration YAML**: Reproducible training configs (learning rate, epochs, LoRA rank, batch size)
- **GPU monitoring logs**: Utilization tracking every 15 seconds with automatic plotting
- **Model comparison reports**: Multi-version offline comparison summaries
- **Experiment design documents**: Hypothesis, metrics, success criteria, rollout plan
- **Experiment Process Templates**: Lifecycle phases from INIT → CLEANING UP

### 4.4 Data Quality & Feature Engineering Artifacts
- **Feature registry YAML**: Centralized Bitbucket configs at project and column levels
- **Feature quality checks**: Zero-value, freshness, volume checks per feature view
- **Data quality pipeline results**: Written to `coreml_feature_quality_profiles` and `coreml_feature_quality_fact` tables
- **Feature metadata**: Descriptions, owners, lineage, materialization schedules
- **Training/serving skew detection**: Monitoring for consistency between offline/online features
- **Data compliance documentation**: PII scrubbing, opt-in/opt-out handling, UGC compliance

### 4.5 Pipeline DAG Configurations
- **ML Studio workflow YAMLs**: Define multi-step pipelines (data prep → training → eval → deployment)
- **Module descriptors** (`module_descriptor.yaml`): Module configuration and parameters
- **Pipeline descriptors** (`pipeline_descriptor.json`): Pipeline integration specs
- **Bitbucket Pipeline configs** (`bitbucket-pipeline.yaml`): CI/CD automation
- **Databricks workflow definitions**: Scheduled execution configs

### 4.6 Deployment & Serving Artifacts
- **Triton `config.pbtxt`**: Dynamic batching, concurrency, instance groups, precision settings
- **Model packaging**: Triton Python backend model + version directory + dependencies
- **Ramp plan documents**: 10% → 50% → 100% schedule with latency monitoring
- **Launch review documents**: User Impact section, metric movements, launch rationale
- **Inference latency budgets**: P90/P99targets per endpoint
- **Auto-scaling configurations**: SageMaker/TEAMServe scaling policies

### 4.7 A/B Test & Experimentation Artifacts
- **Statsig scorecard configurations**: Primary metrics, guardrails, significance thresholds
- **Feature flag definitions**: Kill-switches, progressive rollout gates
- **Experiment design checklists**: Hypothesis, pre-analysis, monitoring, post-analysis
- **Decision logs**: Ship/no-ship rationale with supporting evidence

### 4.8 Training Reproducibility Manifests
- **Model lineage tracking**: Base model → adapter → fine-tuned version chain
- **Dataset versioning**: Point-in-time snapshots with data provenance
- **Environment specifications**: Container definitions (Dockerfile), Python dependencies
- **Hyperparameter search configs**: LoRA rank, learning rate, epochs, batch size, gradient accumulation
- **Multi-node training configs**: MASTER_ADDR, MASTER_PORT, NODE_RANK, NUM_NODES

