## 5. Domain Expertise Areas

### 5.1 NLP / LLM Fine-Tuning (Primary at Atlassian)
- **Techniques**: SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning), LoRA/QLoRA, PEFT, preference optimization (RLHF/DPO)
- **Active use cases**: NL2JQL, NL2Cypher, query rewriting, summarization, content moderation, entity linking
- **Model families**: Llama 3.x (8B, 70B), Phi-3, Mixtral, Gemma, Qwen
- **Key skills**: Dataset curation, prompt engineering, few-shot learning, evaluation design
- **Internal tooling**: `mlp_llm_finetune` module in ML Studio, LLaMA-Factory integration

### 5.2 Search & Ranking Systems (Core Atlassian)
- **Techniques**: Two-tower models, cross-encoders, DCN (Deep & Cross Network), contextual bandits
- **Active use cases**: Jira/Confluence search relevance, 3P document ranking, semantic reranking
- **Key skills**: Learning-to-rank, MRR/NDCG optimization, embedding generation, ANN indexes
- **Scale**: ~198M daily inference requests for similar issues models alone

### 5.3 Recommendation Systems
- **Techniques**: Collaborative filtering, contextual bandits, multi-armed bandits
- **Active use cases**: Next Best Play/Content, notification recommendations, following feed ranking
- **Key skills**: Feature engineering at scale, personalization, A/B testing for recommendations

### 5.4 Computer Vision / Multimodal
- **Active use cases**: Image moderation (SageMaker-hosted), diagram evaluation
- **Key skills**: Image classification, content moderation pipelines, multimodal embeddings

### 5.5 Responsible AI
- **Scope**: Content moderation, policy filtering, bias detection, PII handling
- **Active systems**: Centralized Policy Filter (fine-tuned Llama-3 8B), RAI service
- **Governance**: EU AI Act compliance, ISO 42001 certification, model cards for customers
- **Key skills**: Safety evaluation, red-teaming, bias mitigation, explainability

### 5.6 Distributed Training & Model Optimization
- **Techniques**: FSDP (Fully Sharded Data Parallel), DDP, DeepSpeed (stages1–4), model quantization, TensorRT optimization
- **Active work**: Multi-node training on Databricks/ML Fabric, model compression for serving
- **Key skills**: GPU memory management, communication overhead minimization, mixed-precision training

### 5.7 AIOps / ML for Operations
- **Active use cases**: Anomaly detection, ticket classification, incident prediction, SRE automation
- **Key skills**: Time series analysis, alerting systems, operational ML pipelines

### 5.8 Depth vs. Breadth Balance
Based on Atlassian's ML role distribution data:
- **Applied ML (67%)**: Most MLEs are applied practitioners — deep in1-2 domains, broad across the lifecycle
- **Generalist (19%)**: Comfortable across multiple domains at moderate depth
- **Research (11%)**: Deep in one area, publishing at top venues
- **Infrastructure (3%)**: Systems-focused, deep in serving/training infra

**Recommended balance for a digital MLE**: Deep competence in the assigned model program's domain (e.g., search ranking OR NLP OR recommendations), with broad operational competence across the full ML lifecycle (data → training → eval → deploy → monitor).

