## 6. The Digital MLE Context (AI Employee Application)

The [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727/Digital+MLE+AI+Employee+Vision) maps each responsibility to an autonomy level:

| Activity | Autonomy | Human Role |
|----------|----------|-----------|
| Data freshness monitoring, feature coverage reporting | 🟢 Autonomous | Sets policy, approves new sources |
| Scheduled retraining, model comparison | 🟢 Autonomous | Approves architecture changes |
| Offline eval execution and reporting | 🟢 Autonomous | Makes go/no-go decision |
| Scorecard monitoring, doc drafts | 🟢 Autonomous | Makes launch/rollback decision |
| Serving latency/throughput monitoring | 🟢 Autonomous | Leads incident response |

The digital MLE handles the **instrumentation and reporting work that consumes 50-60% of a senior MLE's week** — freeing human MLEs for research and architectural problems.

