## 3. Cross-Functional Collaboration Patterns

### 3.1 Team Interactions Map

Based on MLE job descriptions and team structures across Atlassian ([P40 MLE](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~455370031/pages/4678981237), [MLSE Lunch and Learning](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121fa4d12f14797451589839ddf71b9d027/pages/4910851230)):

| Partner Team | Collaboration Pattern | Communication Norms |
|-------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **Data Scientists** | Research handoff: DS develops algorithm/approach, MLE productionizes. DS + domain experts handle ideation and experimentation; MLE handles deployment automation and scale. DS works directly with MLE to convert experimentation code into repeatable scripts/jobs. | Shared MLflow experiments, co-design reviews, weekly experiment syncs |
| **Data Engineers** | Feature pipelines: DE manages inputs/outputs, builds data pipeline infrastructure. MLE consumes feature stores (Tecton) and data lakes. DE + MLE collaborate on data quality checks and schema stability. | Data contracts, feature freshness SLAs, pipeline health dashboards |
| **ML Platform Engineers** | Infrastructure partnership: Platform provides compute (ML Fabric), orchestration (ML Studio), serving (TeamServe/MSP), and observability (ML Lens). MLE builds on platform primitives. "Strong ML Engineer and platform partnership" per ML Studio strategy. | Platform office hours, shared SLOs, escalation via Jira, integration feedback loops |
| **SREs / Platform Engineers** | Deployment & reliability: SRE handles infrastructure rollout (Spinnaker, canary analysis), on-call escalation, capacity planning. MLE defines model health signals. Joint ownership of serving reliability. | Shared on-call rotations, incident response runbooks, SLO review cadences |
| **Product Managers** | Success criteria & prioritization: PM defines business metrics, user impact targets, experiment hypotheses. MLE translates to technical constraints. PM reviews experiment results at WEX. | Pre-analysis docs, experiment tracker checklist, Weekly Experimentation Review (WEX) |
| **Security / Compliance** | Model governance: Responsible AI review before production, AI Gateway registration, content filtering/moderation integration, AIMS audit compliance. [GRC-61355](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/GRC-61355) mandates ML standards. | Responsible Technology Review process, AI safety assessments, model cards, audit evidence |
| **Growth / GTM / Finance** | Business stakeholders for ML outcomes: recommendation systems, forecasting, personalization. MLE provides model explanations and business metric attribution. | Quarterly business reviews, impact reporting, dashboard sharing |

### 3.2 Atlassian's MLE Collaboration Model (Microsoft MLOps Level 3)

Per [MLOps Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/VAPPDEV/pages/2166657676):
- **Data scientists**: Working directly with data engineers to convert experimentation code into repeatable scripts/jobs
- **Data engineers**: Working with data scientists and software engineers to manage inputs/outputs
- **Software engineers**: Working with data engineers to automate model integration into application code

### 3.3 Tooling for Collaboration

| Activity | Tools |
|---------|-------|
| Experiment tracking | MLflow, ML Studio, Databricks |
| Feature management | Tecton feature store, ML Feature Store (MLFS) |
| Model serving | TeamServe, SageMaker (MSP), Launchpad |
| Observability | ML Lens, SignalFx, Splunk, Databricks dashboards |
| Experimentation | Statsig + Switcheroo |
| CI/CD | Bitbucket Pipelines, Spinnaker |
| Communication | Slack, Confluence runbooks, Jira epics |

