## 5. Guardrails and Escalation Policies

### 5.1 Automated Guardrails

| Guardrail | Threshold/Mechanism | Action |
|-----------|-------------------|--------|
| **Canary Health Score** | Pass:≥70/100; Marginal (immediate fail): ≤50/100 | Auto-rollback via Spinnaker |
| **Circuit Breaker** | ≥20% failure rate (5xx only) within 60s sliding window, minimum 20calls | Open circuit; exponential backoff (30s base, max 60s); half-open with20 trial probes |
| **Model Health Check** | Post-training: artifact existence + loadability + canary inference passes | HEALTHY → proceed; UNHEALTHY → increment retryCount, apply retry/quarantine logic |
| **Drift Detection** | Statistical tests (KS for numeric, Chi-squared for categorical) against reference window | Alert MLE; trigger evaluation of retraining need |
| **Data Quality SDK** | Null value counts, mean value shifts, volume anomalies | Emit to StreamHub → ML Studio Orchestrator evaluates retraining trigger |
| **Unsafe File Formats** | Block .pkl, .pt, .h5 from production deployment | [COMMIT-27251](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/COMMIT-27251): format validation gates at pipeline level |
| **Training Cost** | Cluster-size × runtime monitoring | Cost dashboards; projected annual savings tracking |
| **SLO Breach** | Per-endpoint SLOs encoded in IaC | Pause experimentation if SLO breached (reliability, latency); SignalFx detectors-as-code |

### 5.2 Approval Gates for Model Promotion

1. **Offline evaluation passes** → automated quality gate (metrics exceed baseline)
2. **Health check pipeline passes** → `ts_launch_validation` annotation recorded in ML Registry
3. **Load test passes** → `ts_loadtest_validation` annotation recorded
4. **Model pre-launch checklist** completed (manual review)
5. **Production capacity confirmed** → manual deployment approval
6. **Canary analysis passes** → automated progressive rollout continues
7. **Responsible AI review** completed for customer-facing models

### 5.3 Escalation Paths

| Trigger | Escalation Path |
|---------|----------------|
| **Model performance degradation detected** | MLE → Team Lead → Platform on-call → Incident (if customer-impacting) |
| **SLO breach during experimentation** | Auto-pause experiment → MLE triage → SRE if infrastructure-related |
| **Circuit breaker tripped (high impact)** | Immediate: Validate in Splunk → Check downstream health → Consider disabling CB for unaffected tenants via feature gate; Document rationale |
| **Responsible AI concerns** | MLE → AI Safety Engineering team → Legal and Compliance (per [AI Governance framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IA/pages/4629430946)) |
| **GPU infrastructure failure** | Platform monitoring detects → MLE notified → ML Platform team owns resolution → Incident if blocking multiple teams |
| **Data pipeline failure** | Automated alerting → DE + MLE joint triage → Incident if impacting model freshness at scale |
| **Cost overrun in training** | Dashboard alert → Team Lead review → Approval required for additional compute |

### 5.4 Responsible AI Escalation

Per [AT-AI-Register-AIMS Objectives](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RM/pages/6709541084):
- All significant AI changes logged in Annual Change Register
- Obtain approval before deployment for AI system changes
- AI Safety incidents target: reduce by 90%
- Model re-evaluation on defined schedule per production AI model
- Nonconformities documented with root cause analysis and corrective actions

