## 4. Common Challenges and Failure Modes

### 4.1 Documented Failure Modes at Atlassian

Based on [Recent challenges with ML Training Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CAIMT/pages/5433466059), [Challenges managing GPU infrastructure](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4407789044), [ML Studio Operational Stability](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5510173634), and [KYC ML Pod - Mechanisms to Scale](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~595679117/pages/6133794933):

| Failure Mode | Description | Impact | Mitigation Strategy |
|-------------|-------------|--------|-------------------|
| **Training Instability** | Same YAML file fails multiple times before success (Mosaic cluster inconsistency); multi-node DDP training significantly slower than single-node (55h vs 1000h+) | 3-4 hours trial-and-error per occurrence | Praxis-ML standardized training recipes; retry/quarantine logic in ML Studio orchestrator; DDP strategy tuning (freeze unused modules, batch right-sizing) |
| **Data/Concept Drift** | Feature distributions shift from training data; label definitions change due to upstream system changes | Silent model degradation → business impact | ML Lens feature drift detection (auto-selects KS/Chi-squared per feature type); automated metric-driven retraining triggers via StreamHub; configurable thresholds |
| **Silent Model Degradation** | Failure is silent — no exceptions, just declining performance. Bugs found months later (stale features from column rename) | Eroded partner confidence; late detection | Analysis notebook templates; Growth Reco distro dashboard; ML Observability migration to ML Lens with alerting; Per-inference SHAP explainability |
| **Feature Store Inconsistencies** | Stale feature service due to column value renames; feature freshness violations; schema changes breaking pipelines | Model serving incorrect predictions | Feature drift dashboards; data quality SDK with null-value/volume/distribution checks; schema validation gates in CI/CD |
| **GPU Resource Contention** | RESOURCE_POOL_EXHAUSTED errors; low-end GPUs insufficient for large models; vCPU rate limiting during peak jobs; Databricks workflow limits (12K) breached | Blocked training; delayed projects | Fallback machine types; capacity reservations; ML Fabric GKE auto-scaling; DCGM monitoring for health (GPU util, memory, ECC errors, NVLink bandwidth) |
| **Dependency/Compatibility Issues** | Nvidia driver updates with unpredictable impact on workloads; constantly evolving ML Platform documentation; unsupported model architectures on platform | 2-3 days debugging; minutes to hours per issue | DCGM GPU Operator for detection; standardized container images; ML Platform API stability commitments; clear versioning |
| **Reproducibility Failures** | Experiments not reproducible from MLflow unless powered by notebook; manual processes lose context | Wasted engineering time; inability to debug regressions | ML Studio auto-creates/reuses experiments per workflow run; full config + metrics tracked; easy to clone and modify existing runs |
| **Monolithic Repository Risk** | ML-UGC repo structure allows non-critical changes to impact core system configurations | Widespread outages (e.g., Databricks group membership deletion, pipeline blocking multiple teams for1+ week) | Repository decomposition ("breaking the monolith"); E2E tests for environment validation; incident-grade response for externally-facing failures |
| **OOM in Training** | GPU framebuffer exhaustion during large model training runs | Job failure requiring manual retry | `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True`; batch right-sizing; cache hygiene; DCGM_FI_DEV_FB_FREE monitoring |
| **Post-Training Hangs** | Workflow hangs after training completion; requires manual termination | Hours of blocked pipeline | Fork + CUDA re-init resolution; fresh single-GPU trainer for post-training eval; timeout guards |
| **Pipeline CI/CD Gap** | Zero automated validation on PR merge — deploys directly to production (observed in core-ml-batch-pipelines) | Any code change immediately in production; no safety net | [ML Pipeline CI/CD Validation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6723101866) proposing linting, data checks, model quality gates |

### 4.2 Systemic Challenges

- **Analyzing ML systems is order of magnitude harder** due to larger surface area: frontend → backend → feature fetching → model inference → deployment → training → data. Failure can be silent. ([KYC ML Pod](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~595679117/pages/6133794933))
- **Contribution measurement gap**: PR count doesn't capture MLE work (15prompt iterations → 3 PRs; 3M data points → 12PRs). Alternative metrics needed: experimentation volume, generated data volume, system efficiency improvements ([Alternative Contribution Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203f8737aa03484f09a4b3f84f0c387eae/pages/5177282593))

